{
  "raw": {
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40572&lang=en": {
      "title": "CLERY Records Evidence Compliance Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 9, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-Police Operations Schedule: Full-time CLERY and Records and Evidence Compliance Specialist Department of Public Safety Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Public Safety Compliance and Records & Evidence Compliance Specialist to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $53,284 - $65,000 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Clery & Evidence Compliance Specialist supports the Department of Public Safety in ensuring compliance with federal, state, and university mandates related to the Jeanne Clery Act, records management, and evidence control. This position exercises sound judgment in managing sensitive data, ensures chain of custody and documentation standards for evidence, and coordinates with police personnel to support both compliance and operational effectiveness. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Clery Compliance (40%) Develop, implement, and maintain Clery Act compliance programs, policies, and reports(Annual Security Report, Fire Safety Report, Daily Crime Log). Coordinate with Campus Security Authorities (CSA), including training and annual compliance letters. Ensure documented proof of compliance for all Clery audits. Act as liaison to campus departments, local law enforcement agencies, and state police to support data sharing and reporting. Provide statistical analysis and trend reports to inform leadership, identify risks, and support strategic planning. Oversee Clery records management to ensure accurate classification, retention, and accessibility of all compliance-related documentation. Collaborate with General Counsel on risk evaluation and policy oversight. Develop, manage, and lead Clery-related committees and working groups to strengthen cross-campus compliance and communication. Assess, build, and implement operational projects and systems that improve Clery compliance and reporting efficiency. Records Custodian- 30% Oversee security, retention, release, and disposition of police records in compliance with state and federal law. Manage Colorado Open Records Act (CORA) requests, including redaction and release processes. Coordinate records requests from law enforcement partners, insurance companies, and community members. Manage NIBRS functions, including coding, data entry, audits, and ensuring timely and accurate monthly submissions to state and federal agencies. Evidence Management- 15% Manage and document chain of custody for all evidence. Catalog and preserve evidence for transfer to crime labs. Ensure officers file evidence accurately in compliance with policy and best practices. Oversee scheduling for evidence review and destruction. Court Liaison- 5% Receive and process all state, municipal, and federal subpoenas. Receive and process Department of Motor Vehicle (OMV) hearing requests. Serve as the primary contact for the 4th Judicial District regarding subpoena updates and officer availability. Serve as the primary contact for the OMV regarding hearing updates and officer scheduling. Serve as the primary contact for the City of Colorado Springs Magistrate's Office for subpoena updates and officer availability. Other Duties- 10% Conduct audits and prepare documentation for compliance reviews. Provide cross-reference support with police personnel to ensure accuracy between records, evidence, and reporting. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the Department's compliance and accountability goals. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 25, 2026 Potential interview dates: November 2 - 6, 2026 Potential start date: December 1, 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41248&lang=en": {
      "title": "Health Care Program Director",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Chanc-Lyda Hill Inst - Hum Res Schedule: Full-time Behavioral Health Program Director Lyda Hill Institute for Human Resilience Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Behavioral Health Program Director to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary : $61,574 - $ 84,929 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Lyda Hill Institute for Human Resilience is seeking a full-time employee to support the development, implementation, and sustainable operations of its Healing Division, which includes the existing Veterans Health and Trauma Clinic (VHTC) and Milestones Resilience Care (MRC) center. The ideal candidate will be adaptable, detail-oriented, and self-directed with excellent communication skills. This role is crucial in supporting our mission to provide high-quality, integrated behavioral health services to our patients and community. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Provide overall direction for the design, development and implementation of sustainable clinical operations of the Healing Division, which include Strategic Plan/Goals development and budgeting. Developing strategic business analyses to improve revenue streams. Monitor and analyze clinic performance metrics, including productivity measures, identifying areas for improvement and recommending solutions. Align operational goals with clinical objectives. Supervise clinic staff and contractors to ensure clinic efficiencies and quality of care. Oversee and provide consultation for VHTC & MRC Contracted Providers. Oversee the client intake process, including scheduling initial appointments and assigning clients to appropriate providers based on clinical needs, availability, and area of expertise. Oversee, document and update space utilization in-clinics. Update and track clinic policies and procedures. Design, implement, and continuously work to improve workflows for client intake, assessment, care planning, and follow-up. Identify and resolve barriers in service delivery. Implement and manage care quality improvement initiatives. Be present in clinic during hours of operation. Develop and maintain efficient scheduling systems for behavioral health providers and support staff to optimize provider schedules, maximize patient access and minimize intake wait times. Electronic Health Record (EHR): audit clinical note codes, times and timeliness, monitor records requests and Request for Services. Ensure Billing Specialist monitors client copayments and payment collections. Prepare, submit, and maintain enrollment, credentialing and recredentialing. Maintain a small clinical case load. Work with marketing coordinator. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 25, 2026 . Potential interview dates: October 26, 2026 - November 6, 2026 . Potential start date: November 9, 2026 . CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41279&lang=en": {
      "title": "Academic Services Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: AA-Campus Extended Studies Schedule: Full-time Academic Services Professional Extended Studies Academic Outreach Department | High School Programs Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier education al institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an Academic Services Professional to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $50,907.00 to $65,686.00 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location : Remote Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary Extended Studies Academic Outreach | High School Programs is an auxiliary unit that operates to extend the resources of the university to the community and beyond by providing highquality undergraduate and graduate courses for traditional and non-traditional students, as well as credit and non-credit professional and personal development experiences. The Academic Services Professional is the primary customer service specialist to provide information and problem solving for internal and external audiences regarding a variety of courses/programs offered through Extended Studies Academic Outreach | High School Programs. This position provides operational support by utilizing various University systems. The Academic Services Professional assists in managing the Noncredit programs and provides operational support for the High School Programs. In addition, this position serves as the primary HR and Financials Liaison for Extended Studies Academic Outreach department. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: 10% Customer Service Assist faculty, staff, students, parents and all customers via phone and email who are seeking information regarding Extended Studies Academic Outreach | High School Programs. 30% Operational Support Manage day-to-day operational office support and contributes to the vision of Extended Studies Academic Outreach department, which provides support for auxiliary courses/programs operated by the colleges and other campus departments. Responsible for accurate data entry of Course Information Sheets (CIS) for Extended Studies Academic Outreach courses, resolves suspended and duplicate applications, generates grade rosters, inputs grades, registrations, drops/withdrawals, utilizes system reports in CU-SIS and other University systems as needed. Communicate and actively engages with Admissions and Records teams regarding application and course scheduling processes to ensure all associated tasks are following University protocol. Communicate with campus departments, regarding procedures and policies for scheduling Extended Studies Academic Outreach courses in CU-SIS. Serve on University and community committees as deemed necessary to accomplish the vision of Extended Studies Academic Outreach initiatives. 20% Extended Studies Program Support Assist in managing noncredit CEU courses Collaborate with campus departments and others to develop, implement and advertise noncredit courses. Update and improve enrollment instructions and websites for noncredit programs. 20% High School Program Support Assist in managing high school programs Communicate with administrators, parents, students regarding program options Update and improve enrollment instructions and websites for high school programs. 10% Human Resources Support HR Liaison for Extended Studies Academic Outreach programs. Creates and processes Letters of Offer, Scope of Work contracts and Person of Interest forms as needed to pay/activate instructors for various Extended Studies Academic Outreach programs. Responsible for accurate data entry in the HCM or PSC system for payments. Attends HR Liaison meetings/updates to ensure all University procedures are followed to efficiently pay individuals who perform services for Extended Studies Academic Outreach programs. 10% Financial & Procurement Support Manages all Procurement Services tasks such as: pcard reconciliation, office supply ordering, creating SPOs and other forms of payment of expenses as needed through CU MarketPlace and Concur Travel system. Assists with Financial tasks such as Creating Journal Entries. Attends Financial Liaison meetings/updates to ensure all University Procedures are followed for Extended Studies Academic Outreach programs. These percentages are estimates. They can change daily, weekly, or monthly depending on work expectations. Please estimate percentage of time based on typical workload. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 16, 2026. Potential interview dates: October 21, 2026 - October 28, 2026. Potential start date: November 11, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41256&lang=en": {
      "title": "Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Wellness Cent./HS&MHS Schedule: Part-time Medical Assistant Wellness Center Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Medical Assistant to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 31,589.00 - $36,176 annually at 80% time . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Non-Exempt fr om the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Wellness Center provides health care services and support to the UCCS student community. The Medical Assistant supports the delivery of safe, efficient, and patient-centered clinical services by performing patient intake, clinical support, laboratory, immunization, and administrative functions. This position works closely with medical providers, students, patients, and campus partners to facilitate timely care, follow-up, and compliance with health requirements. The Medical Assistant uses established clinical protocols, exercises judgment when triaging patient needs, and maintains accurate and confidential patient information and clinical records. The position also supports daily clinic operations, inventory management, infection control, and emergency response activities. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (35%) Patient Care, Intake, and Clinical Support Check in patients and complete required patient intake activities prior to medical provider evaluation. Obtain and document vital signs, health information, and other information required to support patient care, consistent with established clinic procedures. Triage acute care, routine care, and walk-in requests using established protocols and escalate concerns to the appropriate medical provider when indicated. Assist medical providers with examinations, procedures, and other clinical activities within the scope of the position and established protocols. Respond to medical emergencies occurring in the clinic by providing appropriate assistance and support to medical providers until emergency medical personnel arrive. Communicate with patients regarding follow-up examinations, appointments, and other health care needs as directed by the medical provider. Maintain a professional, patient-centered approach when interacting with students and other patients, including individuals seeking urgent or sensitive health care services. (25%) Laboratory, Immunization, and Clinical Testing Collect, label, process, and obtain appropriate laboratory specimens in accordance with clinic procedures and applicable safety requirements. Perform in-house CLIA-waived laboratory testing according to established procedures and quality-control requirements. Monitor laboratory results and notify medical providers when results are received. Track abnormal laboratory results and assist providers with patient follow-up and communication. Notify patients of normal laboratory and radiographic results at the direction of the medical provider. Administer immunizations and injections in accordance with clinic protocols, provider orders, and applicable requirements. Support student compliance with MMR, meningitis, and other applicable immunization or health requirements. Maintain appropriate documentation of immunizations, laboratory testing, and related clinical services. (20%) Clinic Operations, Safety, and Infection Control Maintain adequate medical and clinical supplies by monitoring inventory levels, identifying supply needs, and assisting with supply orders. Stock examination rooms on a routine and as-needed basis to ensure supplies are available for scheduled and unscheduled patient care. Disinfect examination rooms and clinical work areas according to established infection-control procedures. Handle and dispose of biohazardous waste in accordance with applicable safety requirements and clinic procedures. Identify operational or supply issues that may affect patient care and communicate concerns to the appropriate supervisor or provider. Support efficient clinic operations by maintaining organized clinical areas and ensuring equipment and supplies are prepared for patient care. (15%) Patient Communication and Administrative Support Answer telephone calls and assess patient needs to determine the appropriate scheduling or clinical response within established protocols. Schedule appointments based on patient needs and provider availability. Triage walk-in appointment requests and direct patients to the appropriate care or scheduling resource. Communicate with patients regarding laboratory results, follow-up needs, appointments, immunization requirements, and other health care matters as directed. Assist with front desk operations and other administrative activities as needed to maintain efficient daily clinic operations. Coordinate with campus departments and community agencies, as appropriate, to support patient care and health-related services. Protect patient confidentiality and handle health information in accordance with applicable laws, regulations, and university policies. (5%) Documentation, Coordination, and Other Duties Maintain accurate and timely documentation related to patient care, laboratory testing, immunizations, inventory, and other assigned clinical activities. Use independent judgment within established procedures to prioritize competing patient care and clinic operational needs. Collaborate with medical providers and Wellness Center staff to identify and address patient care and operational needs. Participate in required training and maintain knowledge of applicable clinical procedures, university policies, safety requirements, and health care protocols. Perform other related duties as assigned to support the mission and operational needs of the Wellness Center. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 16, 2026 . Potential interview dates: October 21, 2026 - November 6, 2026 . Potential start date: December 1, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41258&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Programmer of Digital Experience, Platforms and Analytics",
      "description": "Posted Date: Oct 1, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-IT Administrative Ops Schedule: Full-time Senior Programmer of Digital Experience, Platforms and Analytics The Office of Information Technology Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Senior Programmer of Digital Experience, Platforms and Analytics to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $66,892.00 - $86,312.00 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: Remote Eligible Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary Reporting to the Assistant Director of Digital Experience, Platforms and Analytics, the Senior Programmer is responsible for the development, enhancement, maintenance, and technical support of enterprise and departmental web applications and digital platforms that support the University’s academic, administrative, and operational needs. This position performs advanced web application development and technical problem-solving within a diverse technology environment, including technologies such as PHP, Drupal, and SQL, and applies established development standards and practices to support secure, accessible, reliable, and sustainable digital services. Working collaboratively with technical teams, campus partners, and other stakeholders, the Senior Programmer analyzes requirements, develops and implements technical solutions, resolves complex application issues, and contributes technical expertise to the continued development and improvement of the University’s digital experience and technology ecosystem. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (50%) Web Application and Drupal Development Analyze, design, develop, test, implement, and maintain web applications, utilities, and digital solutions for the University while complying with applicable industry, University, departmental, accessibility, security, and development standards. Configure, design, and develop schemas, themes, templates, modules, applications, and other functionality within the University’s Drupal Content Management System to support campus departments and University digital services. Convert graphical designs, prototypes, and functional requirements into responsive, accessible, and maintainable web solutions using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, PHP, Drupal, and related web technologies. Develop new functionality and modify, enhance, and integrate functionality within existing web applications and platforms to address changing University and user needs. Develop and maintain database-driven applications and functionality using relational databases, applying knowledge of SQL statements, database normalization, indexing, data structures, and query efficiency. (25%) Application Support, Maintenance and Technical Improvement Provide advanced technical support for web applications and digital platforms, independently diagnosing and resolving complex applications, Drupal, database, integration, configuration, and performance issues. Maintain and enhance existing applications and platforms through software updates, security patches, configuration changes, testing, troubleshooting, and other activities necessary to support reliable, secure, accessible, and sustainable services. Analyze existing applications, code, and technical processes and implement or recommend improvements to functionality, performance, maintainability, accessibility, security, and user experience. Apply and contribute to established development standards and practices, including version control, code review, testing, documentation, deployment, and change management. Research and evaluate emerging technologies, tools, frameworks, and development practices and recommend appropriate solutions for the University’s evolving digital environment. (15%) Technical Leadership and Team Coordination Work with the Assistant Director of Digital Experience, Platforms and Analytics to develop and advance strategic team initiatives, technical priorities, and improvements to the University’s web and digital platform environment. Provide technical guidance, knowledge sharing, and senior-level programming expertise to team members and campus partners within areas of responsibility. Run Web Team meetings as needed to coordinate work, communicate priorities, address technical issues, and support progress on team initiatives. Assign and communicate work priorities to student employees on the Web Team; provide technical direction and guidance necessary to support completion of assigned work. Contribute to technical planning, application architecture, development standards, reusable solutions, and decisions regarding the implementation and long-term support of web applications and digital platforms. (10%) Project Collaboration and Campus Partnership Consult and collaborate with campus departments, stakeholders, and technology teams to understand business needs, gather requirements, evaluate technical options, and develop appropriate web and digital solutions. Participate in project planning, estimation, prioritization, implementation, testing, deployment, and ongoing support of assigned initiatives. Communicate technical requirements, recommendations, risks, and solutions clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders. Maintain appropriate technical documentation for applications, configurations, integrations, development processes, and ongoing support. Coordinate application changes, releases, and other production activities with appropriate team members, campus partners, and vendors. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: Sunday, October 4, 2026 @ 11:59pm. Potential interview dates: October 7, 2026 - October 9, 2026. Potential start date: November 1, 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41263&lang=en": {
      "title": "Temporary Payroll Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-RM-Human Resources Schedule: Part-time Temporary Payroll Specialist Office of Human Resources Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Temporary Payroll Specialist to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary/Pay Range : $27 - $34 hourly . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Non-Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-site/Hybrid/In-state Remote Benefits at a Glance Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! CU Advantage Summary The Human Resources Assistant supports the Human Resources Operations team during the PeopleSoft Time & Labor implementation. This position will take on various tasks related to the legacy timekeeping system and other duties related to this project implementation. This position requires a strong awareness of data integrity, attention to confidentiality, and the ability to navigate complex HRIS systems and processes in support of campus-wide HR functions. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (95%) Human Resources Operations Uses Oracle PeopleSoft HR system HCM to provide accurate and timely entry of appointments into the HCM system for payroll, and ensure accuracy and compliance with hiring, promotional, and additional compensation rules and guidelines for faculty, university staff, and classified staff appointments. Completes background and misconduct checks for job candidates. Updates non-person profiles and person profiles and other data entry and clean up for effective launch of Time and Labor. Completes required quality assurance testing for Time & Labor project. Coordinates and processes employment change letters related to the Time & Labor project, such as changes to pay roll frequency or pay rate. Executes data quality audits (e.g., I-9 reverifications, payroll registers, pay change reports, timecard follow-up), proactively correcting discrepancies. Maintains data integrity through regular system reconciliation and by identifying systemic issues for continuous improvement. Supports operational surges by processing new hires, separations, and other workforce transactions in collaboration with the HR Operations team. (5%) Other Duties Contribute to ad hoc HR initiatives and special projects requiring collaboration, research, or administrative execution. May conduct training for the launch of Time & Labor. Tentative Search Timeline Priority w ill be given to applications submitted by: 10/11/2026 . Potential interview dates: 10/12/2026 - 10/23/2026. Potential start date: 11/1/2026 . CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41266&lang=en": {
      "title": "Digital Content Strategist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSIO-Admin Schedule: Full-time Digital Content Strategist University Communications & Marketing Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Digital Content Strategist to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary/Pay Range : $ 55,954 - $65,000 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site/Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary: The Digital Content Strategist plays a key role in shaping and executing the digital content strategy for UCCS’ flagship website, uccs.edu and other supporting platforms and channels. In this position you will: Monitor content performance metrics and use data to guide decision-making. Develop audience-centered, digital-first content that enhances the user experience. Support student enrollment goals through strategic content creation. Ensure all content reflects and strengthens the institution’s brand voice. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver engaging, high-value content. Drive user engagement, conversion, and long-term audience growth. Analyze web analytics and user insights to identify opportunities for improvement. Optimize content performance through continuous testing and refinement. Translate data and user behavior trends into actionable strategic recommendations. Contribute to marketing strategy as a key member of the marketing team. Establish and maintain content governance standards and best practices. Promote brand consistency across digital channels and content platforms. Enhance the customer experience through effective content strategy and management. Foster a culture of innovation, continuous improvement, and data-informed decision-making. Support the goals and initiatives of the Marketing Director. Position Term This is a one-year full time position within University Communications & Marketing. The position is intended to provide digital content support for university marketing and communications priorities during the one year period. Continuation beyond the one-year is not guaranteed and would be subject to university needs, funding, and applicable hiring processes. Essential Functions: The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (40% Operations Management) Deep Digital Content Expertise: Extensive experience developing and executing content strategy, digital marketing initiatives, and higher education web content that align customer needs with business objectives and drive measurable engagement. Strong Leadership & Operational Excellence: Proven ability to lead people, processes, and cross-functional projects while continuously improving workflows, establishing best practices, and managing complex content initiatives from strategy through execution. Distributed Environment Experience: Demonstrated success working across teams and decentralized organizations, effectively navigating multiple stakeholders, priorities, and compliance requirements. Data-Driven Decision Making: Strong analytical skills with experience leveraging web analytics, performance metrics, and customer insights to identify trends, optimize content strategies, improve user experience, and influence business outcomes. Exceptional Communicator & Storyteller: Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to create compelling customer-centric narratives, simplify complex concepts, engage diverse audiences, and clearly articulate business value. Bachelor’s degree in digital marketing, Communications, or a related field required. Develop, implement, and continuously improve digital content strategies that align with institutional goals, brand standards, customer needs, and student enrollment objectives. Manage the full content lifecycle from ideation through implementation, ensuring consistency, accessibility, compliance with legal and regulatory requirements, and adherence to content governance standards. Create, optimize, and maintain digital content across web and digital platforms to enhance user experience, increase engagement, drive traffic, and support lead generation and enrollment outcomes. Analyze content performance using web analytics, SEO, AEO/GEO, and other digital marketing tools to evaluate effectiveness, identify opportunities, and implement data-informed improvements. Establish and refine content management processes, workflows, and best practices that support operational efficiency, brand consistency, and long-term content sustainability. Monitor emerging trends, technologies, and industry best practices in digital marketing, content strategy, search optimization, and user experience to enhance content effectiveness and organizational outcomes. (35% Communication and Collaboration) Collaborate with Marketing, Enrollment Management, Web Services, UI/UX teams, Communications, Admissions, Institutional Data, and other campus stakeholders to ensure cohesive messaging and alignment of content strategies. Partner with cross-functional teams to develop customer-centric content and digital experiences that support institutional priorities and business objectives. Serve as a strategic advisor by translating analytics, customer insights, and performance metrics into actionable recommendations for stakeholders and leadership. Develop compelling narratives and content that effectively communicate institutional value, engage diverse audiences, and strengthen the university's brand presence. Facilitate communication among decentralized teams and stakeholders to ensure content initiatives are coordinated, compliant, and aligned with organizational goals. (25% Administrative Tasks) Maintain content governance documentation, standards, procedures, and reporting processes to support compliance, consistency, and accountability across digital platforms. Prepare and present content performance reports, recommendations, and strategic updates to leadership and stakeholders. Coordinate project timelines, priorities, and deliverables for content-related initiatives, ensuring projects are completed on schedule and within established guidelines. Track key performance indicators (KPIs), user engagement metrics, and enrollment-related outcomes to support strategic planning and continuous improvement efforts. Participate in professional development activities and maintain knowledge of evolving digital content, marketing, accessibility, and higher education industry standards. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 11, 2026 . Potential interview dates: October 14, 2026 - October 21. 2026. Potential start date: November 1, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41260&lang=en": {
      "title": "Graphic Design Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCSIO-Admin Schedule: Full-time Graphic Design Specialist University Communications & Marketing Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Graphic Design Specialist to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary/Pay Range : $44,567 - $57,506 annually. Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site/Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Graphic Design Specialist supports the University Marketing and Communications team through the development of creative, high-quality print and digital communications aligned with UCCS strategic goals and brand standards. Provides print and digital design support for university communications and marketing initiatives. Develops creative solutions that advance the university’s strategic communication objectives. Promotes a positive image of UCCS to prospective students, alumni, donors, and other key constituents. Researches, designs, and produces high-quality printed and electronic communications materials. Creates multimedia content critical to advancing the university’s mission. Ensures all materials align with UCCS brand standards and visual design guidelines. Position Term This is a one-year full time position within University Communications & Marketing. The position is intended to provide graphic design support for university marketing and communications priorities during the one year period. Continuation beyond the one-year is not guaranteed and would be subject to university needs, funding, and applicable hiring processes. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (20% Operations Management) Design and produce on-brand digital and print collateral, including flyers, advertisements, invitations, annual reports, event programs, and other materials as needed. Develop creative concepts and design plans that support university strategic communication goals across print, digital, and multimedia platforms. Handle production and preflight of final print-ready artwork using InDesign, Photoshop, Illustrator, and other appropriate design software; ensure proper sizing, resolution, formatting, and technical specifications of imagery and other design elements. Translate design elements effectively between digital and print media while maintaining visual consistency and adherence to UCCS brand standards. Apply current industry standards, design trends, and technical knowledge to create high-quality, effective communications materials. Perform detailed work with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail throughout the design and production process. (40% Communication & Collaboration) Attend client meetings, as necessary, to determine communication needs; research, develop, present, and refine design concepts based on client objectives and audience needs. Work with the Brand and Design Manager to ensure proper implementation of brand standards and visual design, including receiving final approval from the Marketing and Communications team on highly visible campaigns and design concepts. Collaborate with cross-discipline teams and clients to develop integrated multimedia projects and effectively manage competing project priorities and individual workloads. Give and receive direction, feedback, and constructive criticism while iterating on design work within established brand standards and communication objectives. Communicate effectively with clients, colleagues, and stakeholders regarding project requirements, timelines, revisions, and deliverables. Adapt to changing priorities, deadlines, and client needs while maintaining a high level of quality and professionalism. Provide creative input and expertise in areas including concept development, design planning, art/photo direction, print design, digital design, and multimedia production. Support a collaborative work environment by exhibiting objectivity and openness to others' views and perspectives. (40% Administrative Tasks) Design and produce final artwork for print and digital paid media campaigns across multiple platforms and formats. Provide desktop publishing and graphic design support to university staff and departments. Assist in the development and production of templates, digital assets, and other reusable communications resources. Manage multiple projects simultaneously while maintaining established deadlines, priorities, and quality standards. Organize and maintain design files and digital assets in accordance with established file management and digital asset management practices. Utilize a broad range of design programs and platforms, including InDesign, Photoshop, Illustrator, Lightroom, Canva, and other Adobe Creative Suite and graphic design/interactive software as appropriate. Incorporate photography and photo-editing techniques into design projects, as appropriate. Maintain awareness of emerging design tools, technologies, industry standards, and trends to support continuous improvement of university communications. Perform other related duties as assigned in support of the University Marketing and Communications team. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 11, 2026. Potential interview dates: October 14, 2026 - October 23, 2026. Potential start date: November 1, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41257&lang=en": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 29, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Academic Advising Schedule: Full-time Academic Advisor Academic Advising This position is dependent on the availability of funding. Funding is currently expected to last 2 years. Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Academic Advisor to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary $ 42,355 - $54,651 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: Hybrid Eligible Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary Partnering with students to successfully navigate college is the mission of Academic Advising at the University of Colorado Colorado Springs. Academic advisors at UCCS accomplish this mission by providing high-quality, personalized, and comprehensive advising to degree-seeking students from orientation through graduation. Advisors partner with students and the campus community to empower students to take ownership of their education and be successful in college. Advisors support and challenge students in their learning and development by: Providing practical and developmental guidance that respects each student’s individual path. Facilitating student exploration and navigation of educational and personal goals. Developing strategies for student success in college and connecting students to opportunities and resources available for their growth. Helping students to develop self-authorship and personal responsibility and to value higher education as they engage in their educational journey. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Provide proactive and developmental academic advising to undergraduate students by analyzing student’s career and academic goals, degree progress, deficiencies and test results, and by recommending appropriate course of action or referrals. Interpret and communicate accurate information about campus policies and degree requirements. Support new student enrollment by providing intake appointments and packets for orientation, help students register for their first semester of classes, and provide follow-up and regular communication from orientation through the start of the first semester of classes. Evaluate transfer credits from other colleges for application toward undergraduate degree programs by determining how the transfer courses equate to our requirements. Work closely with academic and other departments while providing outstanding customer service. Determine how to best facilitate the student’s success and development and provide advising that improves overall student retention. Contribute to the success of the department and University by abiding by team norms, accomplishing tasks affecting other team members in a timely manner, work closely with team members in creating presentations and advising resources, and representing Academic Advising in a professional way at all times. Appropriately document all contact with students, including appointment notes, email, and phone conversations. Actively participate in department initiatives for student success, early alert outreach, and intervention. Collaborate with campus departments and partners such as Career Services and Orientation to support student success. Proactively manage a caseload of students by utilizing technology to identify students in need of advising support, communicating regularly with students, and connecting students to the resources and opportunities to help them engage and find belonging at UCCS. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 6, 2026. Potential interview dates: Week of October 12-16, 2026 . Potential start date: November 1, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41123&lang=en": {
      "title": "IT Systems Administrator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 24, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-IT Administrative Ops Schedule: Full-time IT Professional/ IT Systems Administrator The Office of Information Technology Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an IT Systems Administrator to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $62,856 - $81,105 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary This position primarily supports the VMware and Linux server/workstation environment. This position is responsible for monitoring of systems and applications, assisting with client workstation issues, maintaining system and account integrity, and supporting senior system administrators with tasks related to system performance, network issues, and system configuration. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Systems Administration (50%) Configuring Linux and Windows servers. Collaborate with and support senior staff and administrators in overall systems management. Assist with configuration and integration of other technology into an Active Directory domain environment. Assist with administration of Red Hat (CentOS, Stream, Fedora, Alma, Rocky) servers on VMware, bare metal, and containers. Assist with administration of VMware vSphere clusters and ESXi hosts. Perform Maintenance and troubleshooting on existing Linux and VMware install base. Perform and assist with software installs using automation tools. Write Ansible playbooks and bash scripts for system maintenance. Monitoring and Incident response (30%) Perform basic security auditing of system architecture. Support senior system administrators with security configuration and security incidents. Proactive monitor systems for performance issues using native and third party tools. Monitoring ticketing system for escalations. Provide second and third level support for ticket escalations from the IT HelpDesk. Escalate support tickets when necessary and seek guidance from senior administrators/staff. Research (10%) Work with senior administrators to manage and monitor slurm and HPC jobs. Help faculty and students use research related systems. Work on incidents related to research-based systems. Administrative (10%) Document all work completed. Track project milestones, deliverables, and documentation to ensure timely completion. Train users on systems. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: Sunday, October 11, 2026 at 11:59pm. Potential interview dates: October 19, 2026 - November 5, 2026. Potential start date: December 1, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41095&lang=en": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Associate",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 23, 2026 Job category: Research Faculty Department: EAS-Computer Science Schedule: Full-time The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position Post Doctoral Associate Department of Computer Science College of Engineering and Applied Science Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Post Doctoral Associate to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 65,000 - $ 75,000 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. This position is dependent on the availability of fudning which is expected to last 6 months. Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The post-doctoral researcher will work in the Laboratory for Cybersecurity Dynamics, under the supervision of the Lab Director, Professor Shouhuai Xu. This position will work on challenging but exciting space cybersecurity research problems, collaborate with PhD students who work on the same or related problems, mentor junior student researcher, and lead efforts in writing top-quality scientific/academic research papers for top-venue publications. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: This position is a 100% research and development position. This position will tackle challenging space cybersecurity research problems that require high creativity and ability to conduct original research, with strong publication record. This position is required to design new cybersecurity solutions (e.g., architectures) and characterize their properties, both of which demand analytical thinking and skills. This position is dependent on the availability of internal grant funding. Funding is currently expected to last nine months. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: September 26, 2026. Potential interview dates: week of October 5, 2026. Potential start date: October 15 or November 1, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41085&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Computer Science",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 22, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: EAS-Computer Science Schedule: Full-time The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position Assistant Teaching Professor Department of Computer Science College of Engineering and Applied Science Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Assitant Teaching Professor to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 69,000 - $75,000 per academic year. Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Benefits at a Glance Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! CU advantage Summary This teaching assistant professor position will teach undergraduate courses possibly including cross-listed courses in the Department of Computer Science as assigned by the department chair. The typical course load for an instructor is 24 credit hours (80% time) per academic year and service activity (20% time). Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: An individual hired for this position will teach courses necessary for multiple Computer Science (CS) and related degrees and specializations. Activities include: Teaching undergraduate, and possibly cross-listed, courses in cybersecurity and computer science Developing new courses in computer science Advising undergraduate majors Participating in College and Departmental committees and meetings Other activities as assigned by the Chair of the Computer Science Department Additional activities may include: Guiding undergraduate students in independent studies Developing and teaching online courses. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 5, 2026. Potential interview dates: week of November 1, 2026. Potential start date: January 11, 2027 or August 16, 2027. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41125&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Assessment and Crisis",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Wellness Cent./HS&MHS Schedule: Full-time Assistant Director of Assessment and Crisis Wellness Center Mental Health Services (WCMHS) Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an Assistant Director of Assessment and Crisis to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 75 ,000.00 - $100 ,000.00 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: Hybrid Eligible Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary This position provides both clinical and non-clinical services. Clinical services entail clinical psychology and counseling services to UCCS students, whose personal/emotional life interferes with their ability to perform academically. The direct clinical services include: Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include but are not limited to the following: Directly responsible for development, and execution of our neuropsychological offerings at the WCMHS including the educational materials around all neuropsychological testing. This position will change or adapt our offerings as the need arises around neuropsychology. Additionally, responsible for creating an annual budget and managing both income and expenses for all assessment needs to operate all testing services. Responsible for all testing online materials, equipment needed, and pen/paper assessments. Expanding assessment services and tools throughout all mental health services. Partner with the WCMHS Director of Clinical Training (DCT) to provide training and supervision for trainees who participate in the testing services. Partner with UCCS Disability Services team for testing services that impact accommodations for UCCS students and provide the most up to date education to the Disability Servies team. Develop a crisis/emergency plan, train all staff/trainees on the process, and regularly evaluate the effectiveness of the plan and along with remaining up to date on most current research around college campus crisis/emergency needs. Respond to psychological crises/emergency walk ins or calls to the WCMHS; be available to make assessments; and carry out crisis/emergency interventions; in addition to contribute to on-call duties of the WCMHS clinicians. Responsible for developing and implementing data collection strategies to keep track of various Mental Health Service data to help contribute to data collection of services provided by the WCMHS, analyze the collected data to be able to inform service decisions based on outcomes information, and assist with billing of non-Wellness Center units/agencies when needed. Psychotherapy services in individual therapy, group therapy, couple therapy, and family therapy formats. Whenever clinically necessary, make appropriate referrals to on- and off campus services and being available to contribute to case consultations with these agencies. Whenever there are referrals (both general and mandatory) from other offices in the university for services (i.e. education/outreach, counseling, and evaluations), providing the required support service and/or assisting other clinicians in carrying out the request as needed. As WCMHS accepts graduate students, predoctoral psychology interns and post-doctoral fellows from psychology, social work and counseling programs from both UCCS and other schools, sharing the clinical supervision load of these students with other clinicians. Regularly participate in supervision consultation and training. Attend all the staff meetings and administrative meetings that are related to position's responsibilities. Maintain accurate information on the WCMHS website as well as take the lead on WCMHS materials used around campus. Partake in the WCMHS staffs’ efforts to organize and coordinate campus-wide education and prevention programs and assist in efforts to address the developmental needs of the campus. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 5, 2026. Potential interview dates: October 9, 2026 - October 14, 2026. Potential start date: November 15, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41168&lang=en": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 18, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Intercolleg Athletics Schedule: Part-time Assistant Athletic Trainer Intercollegiate Athletics Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Assistant Athletic Trainer to j oin our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary/Pay Range : $ 40.00 - $45.00 hourly . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Non-Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location : On-Site Benefits at a Glance Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! CU Advantage Because this appointment is temporary, you will not be eligible to receive all of the benefits normally provided to members of the university staff under the standard University of Colorado benefits programs. You are not eligible to receive paid vacation leave, medical, or retirement benefits. However, you are eligible to accrue sick leave and you will accrue 0.034 hours of sick leave per hour worked. Summary Under the general guidance and supervision of the Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Medicine, Director of Athletics, and Team Physicians, the Assistant Athletic Trainer supports comprehensive athletic medicine services through injury care, medical coordination,recordkeeping, and daily clinic operations while contributing to athlete wellbeing and performance outcomes across intercollegiate programs. This position is temporary and expected to last no more than 9 months. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: 55% Manage all aspects of prevention, evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries for approximately 370 student-athletes at UCCS and on the road. 25% Maintain updated files and accurate medical records of the following: athletic injuries,medical insurance, medical history, injury referrals, conditioning programs, schedules, and other necessary data. 10% Maintain regular clear communication between athletic medicine staff, coaches, student athletes, and other UCCS employees as needed to ensure the safety and wellbeing of the student athletes. 5% Coordinate clinical and physician appointments between the athlete and UCHealth or outside referral. 5% Performs other duties as assigned. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: 9/21/2026 . Potential interview dates: 9/22/2026. Potential start date: 9/23/2026 . CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41129&lang=en": {
      "title": "Student Support Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 18, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Dean Of Students Schedule: Full-time Student Support Specialist Office of the Dean of Students Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Student Support Specialist to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $44,729.00 - $57,715.00 Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site/Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Office of the Dean of Students cultivates student success through student support and advocacy, educational opportunities, and the promotion of personal accountability and empowerment. The Office of the Dean of Students' addresses issues of students’ safety and wellbeing, and we support all students in times of challenge and crisis. Primary responsibilities for this positions include: risk assessment for incoming referrals, administering academic withdrawal process for students with extenuating circumnutates, implementing interventions determined by the CARE Team, providing support and case management services to non-crisis referrals and supporting CARE Team administrative operations. This position is dependent on the availability of funding. Funding is currently expected to last 3 years. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Student Support (55%) Serve as a departmental representative of the CARE Team. Provide administrative support to CARE Team meetings, including but not limited to taking case management notes and providing appropriate follow-up documentation. At the direction of CARE Team, respond to students in crisis. This may include providing resource referrals, academic support/planning, communicating with faculty, on-going wellbeing check-ins, communicating with concerned family members, and ensuring students receive proper follow ups. Manage personal caseload with minimal oversight from supervisor. Manage low-concern CARE Team cases related to students living on-campus. Provide case management services to students who are experiencing difficulties that may include, but are not limited to: academic performance, physical and/or psychological health/wellness, as well as interpersonal relationships. This function involves assisting students as they navigate various University offices and processes; consulting with and gathering information from internal and external resources to support the holistic wellbeing of students; advocating for students and their needs to campus constituents; and properly documenting all case interactions. Academic Withdrawals (30%) Manage most, if not all, academic withdrawal requests through the Office of the Dean of Students. Assist students facing extenuating circumstances through the late or retroactive withdrawal process and referring the student to various support measures on and off campus. Assess all incoming withdrawal requests for urgent/emergent factors that may require escalation. Collect and compile data related to the academic withdrawal process. Provide feedback and suggestions on how to improve the process overall. Recommend academic withdrawals decision to both supervisor and college specific Associate Deans. Assists students in determining reentry strategies after their immediate crisis/emergency is resolved. Office Support and Administration (15%) Assess student complaints for appropriate referral within the Office of the Dean of Students or to campus partners. Provide immediate support to walk-in concerns, assessing for urgent/emergent needs, deescalating when appropriate, and providing next-step solutions to students. Assist in the data collection and assessment for CARE Team report preparation. Represent the Office the Dean of Students on various standing or ad hoc committees as assigned. Support campus wide events such as orientation and commencement. Other duties as assigned Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: 10/04/2026 Potential interview dates: 10/09/2026 - 10/16/2026 Potential start date: 11/01/2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41143&lang=en": {
      "title": "Philanthropic Strategy and Principal Gifts Officer",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 18, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCUA-University Development Schedule: Full-time Philanthropic Strategy and Principal Gifts Officer University Development Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Philanthropic Strategy and Principal Gifts Officer to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $127,378 - $155,000 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary University Advancement builds support and affinity for UCCS through coordinated community engagement, alumni outreach, donor relations, and strategic partnerships. The Philanthropic Strategy and Principal Gifts Officer leads the development and securement of significant and principal gifts in partnership with the campus senior leadership team. The Officer collaborates closely with Advancement colleagues, campus leadership and central advancement staff to strategically coordinate engagement, cultivation and stewardship for the university's most significant donors who are interested in supporting UCCS' strategic priorities aligned with campus and division priorities. This position is critical in securing lead gifts, leading strategy for top prospects, peer mentoring, and partnering with development staff to scale major gifts support and is responsible for implementing vision for targeted initiatives by co-developing strategy. This role ensures cohesive donor-centric fundraising guidance across the organization, while also managing a personal portfolio of high-capacity donors to secure major and principal gifts. This position promotes a culture of teamwork around shared and individual success, advances a donor-centric culture, drives pipeline development, and supports cross-functional initiatives across engagement, philanthropy, and public-private partnerships, leveraging leadership influence. Through leadership, collaboration, and disciplined portfolio management, the Philanthropic Strategy and Principal Gifts Officer strengthens philanthropic investment in UCCS and enhances the institution’s long-term trajectory of advancement. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (65%) Fundraising & Donor Portfolio Management Manage a personal portfolio of approximately 50+ high-capacity prospects capable of making major and principal gifts. Lead and contribute to UCCS strategy for a cross-campus portfolio of 50+ high-capacity prospects capable of making major and principal gifts. Identify, cultivate, solicit, and close significant complex gifts from individuals, corporations, and foundations to advance institutional mission and strategic initiatives. Develop individualized strategies for engaging and stewarding high-net-worth donors and organizational partners; conduct initial engagement (e.g., cold outreach) where appropriate. Cultivate new and existing relationships to build, sustain, and deepen affinity with donors, alumni, corporate partners, and community leaders to grow philanthropic investment. Lead and assist in the development of complex proposals for soliciting individual, corporate, or foundation prospects, using knowledge from varied sources to ensure they are accurate and complete. Meet personal fundraising performance goals while supporting the achievement of team-wide fundraising outcomes. Collaborate with the Portfolio Intelligence team to evaluate prospects, analyze giving potential, and strengthen UCCS’s overall prospect pool. In coordination with Donor Relations, develop and implement enhanced bespoke stewardship strategies for significant donors and coordinate engagement actions with the appropriate office (President, Provost, Dean, etc.) and Advancement Foundation. (25%) Strategic Fundraising Leadership Provide peer coaching and strategic fundraising guidance for the Major Gifts team in partnership with the Vice Chancellor for Advancement and Engagement (VCAE) and the Sr. Director of Development in alignment with fundraising priorities, institutional and advancement goals. Foster a collaborative, mission-driven, donor-centric culture grounded in best practices, innovation, accountability, and shared purpose. Support the Chancellor and Vice Chancellor for Advancement and Engagement in securing top-level donor commitments by leading internal campus collaborative conversations, gaining institutional support and structures to implement philanthropic initiatives or programs. Collaborate with the Vice Chancellor for Advancement and Engagement and Division leadership to establish fundraising and engagement strategies for colleges, divisions, programs, and institutional initiatives. Responsible for leading assigned strategies through influence and collaboration across the organization and within the community. Selectively partner with division leadership to support operational modeling, workflow improvements, and project-based initiatives that enhance efficiency and unit impact. Contribute to cross-functional initiatives to strengthen the major-gift pipelines and public private partnerships. Represent University Advancement and Engagement at CU System events, campus committees, and high-level leadership engagements as needed. (10%) Operational Accountability & Data Integrity Manage multiple, complex tasks simultaneously while anticipating deadlines and maintaining proactive communication with stakeholders. Ensure timely, accurate documentation of development activity, including strategies, contact reports, proposals, pledges, and fund agreements, in accordance with institutional and industry standards (e.g., Donor Bill of Rights). Maintain strict confidentiality and uphold all professional and ethical standards in donor engagement. Use CRM systems and Microsoft Office tools to support analysis, reporting, portfolio development, and team management. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 1, 2026 Potential virtual first round interview dates: October 6-8, 2026 Potential in-person second round interview dates: October 12-14, 2026 Potential start date: November 1, 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41121&lang=en": {
      "title": "Student Activities and Engagement Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 17, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Student Life Operating Schedule: Full-time Student Activities and Engagement Program Manager Student Life and Leadership Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier education al institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Student Activities and Engagement Program Manager to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary/Pay Range : $ 47,351- 60,000 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site/Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Program Manager, Student Activities and Engagement will lead long-term and short-term strategic visioning and planning for student engagement and advocate for departmental needs and resources to support student engagement. The Program Manager, Student Activities and Engagement is responsible for planning, implementing, promoting, and assessing a comprehensive portfolio of student engagement opportunities that foster involvement, belonging, retention, persistence, and student success. Reporting to the Director of Student Engagement, this position coordinates campus traditions, educational programs, entertainment events, and community-building initiatives that serve residential, commuter, and nontraditional students. The position develops collaborative partnerships across the university, leads marketing and outreach efforts, supervises student employees, and utilizes assessment data to continuously improve programs and services. Frequent evening and weekend work is required. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: 45% Student Activities and Campus Programming Coordinate and assess student engagement programs and campus traditions. Direct and manage a full calendar of large-scale, traditional events on campus, including, but not limited to, Clyde’s Kickoff, Disorientation Week, Homecoming Weekend, Winter Welcome Week, Commuter Appreciation Weeks, and other related co-sponsored events. Develops and facilitates ongoing weekly programs and events that engage a broad cross-section of the student body. Emphasis will be placed on hosting events in a wide variety of campus locations and beyond Lead collaborative and inclusive campus programing efforts with students, administrators, faculty, staff, and the community. Manage logistics, contracts, vendors, staffing, and evaluations. Coordinate commuter student engagement initiatives. In partnership with Residence Life and Housing staff, expand active and engaging student programming within the residential villages. 25% Marketing, Communications, and Student Outreach Develop marketing and promotional strategies. Maintain engagement platforms, calendars, social media, websites, and digital signage. Ensure alignment with university branding standards. Oversee the capture of high-resolution photos and videos at student events and develops promotional strategies that showcase these experiences through Student Life & Leadership and UCCS communication channels, including social media, websites, digital signage, print publications, and other outreach platforms. 15% Assessment and Program Evaluation Track participation and attendance data. Administer evaluations and surveys. Incorporate program and learning outcomes into a robust calendar of programs and events. Prepare reports and recommendations for continuous improvement. Actively serve on the campus programming committee 15% Supervision and Departmental Support Recruit, train, supervise, and evaluate student employees. Provide active supervision, leadership development, and mentoring. Participate in departmental initiatives and perform related duties Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 11th, 2026 . Potential interview dates: October 20th-22nd, 2026 Potential 2nd interview dates: October 27th- 28th, 2026 Potential start date: November 16th, 2026 . CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41087&lang=en": {
      "title": "Instruction & Research Librarian",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 15, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: AA-Library Operations Schedule: Full-time The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position Instruction and Research Librarian (Instructor Rank) Kraemer Family Library Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an Instruction and Research Librarian to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary/Pay Range : $ 50,000 - $55,000 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location : On-Site/Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary As a faculty member of the Learning, Research, and Engagement Department, the Instruction & Research Librarian provides information literacy instruction and research assistance in various formats to the UCCS community. The following job duties are expected but not all-inclusive. This position may explore additional interests in developing, delivering, and promoting library services or be asked to take on other duties as assigned. This is a 12-month faculty appointment that requires commitments in the areas of Teaching/Librarianship and Leadership and Service. Scholarly/Creative Work is not required. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Provide in person and/or online information literacy instruction in the First-Year Rhetoric and Writing Program, Gateway Program Seminar, and library workshops. This may include night and weekend classes. Provide general research assistance service in-person and through remote formats. Participate in the development and maintenance of online learning materials. Assist with assessment of library instruction and research assistance activities. Serve as a liaison to academic divisions or departments in the College of Education or other assigned area providing collection development, library instruction, and research assistance. Participate in the development of policies, procedures, and goals for the Learning, Research, and Engagement department and the Kraemer Family Library. Demonstrate a commitment to the academic or campus community through library, campus, CU System, or professional service activities. The job duties Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 25, 2026 . Potential interview dates: November 2, 2026 - December 11, 2026 . Potential start date: January 1, 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and compl ies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40717&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Nursing",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 14, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Beth-El UG Nursing Schedule: Full-time The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position Assistant Teaching Professor, Nursing Department of Nursing Helen and Arthur E. Johnson Beth-El College of Nursing and Health Sciences Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an Assistant Teaching Professor to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 50,000 - $64,000 per a cademic year. Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt fro m the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Benefits at a Glance Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! CU advantage Summary This is a full-time, 9-month, on-campus, non-tenure track appointment at the Assistant Teaching Professor level with 80% teaching and 20% service work distribution in the Department of Nursing. This position is expected to teach 24 credit hours per academic year and includes responsibilities in the undergraduate programs; and conduct classroom, clinical, and online teaching. Faculty also participate in both internal and external professional service activities and demonstrate collaborative interests and collegiality in all aspects of faculty engagement. The position includes classroom, online, laboratory/simulation, and clinical teaching with lead responsibility for courses in adult health nursing. In addition to the 9-month academic year, the faculty has an opportunity to teach during the summer session for additional compensation. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Provide instruction to undergraduate students in the classroom, static lab, simulation learning center, online, and clinical settings. Engage in various service activities within the department, college, UCCS, the profession of nursing, and the community. Maintain clinical and academic expertise. Select and schedule student learning experiences to achieve desired learning outcomes. Plan, develop, and implement evaluation tools to assess student progress. Participate in curriculum development, implementation, and evaluation. Participate in meetings and other activities that advance the mission and goals of the department and college. Other duties as determined by the Dean and Department Chair. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: October 4, 2026 . Potential interview dates: October 12-November 6, 2026. Potential start date: December 2026. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40983&lang=en": {
      "title": "Custodian II",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 11, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-FAC-ADMIN OP Schedule: Full-time Custodian II/ Custodial Lead Facilities Services Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier education al institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Custodial Lead to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 36,122 - $46,609 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Non-Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Custodian II – Custodial Lead provides comprehensive cleaning, sanitation, and facility support services across a wide range of campus environments, including academic buildings, research laboratories, offices, student centers, dining facilities, and high-traffic public spaces. This position ensures all areas are safe, clean, and well-maintained to support teaching, research, student engagement, and campus life. The role supports both routine operations and campus events, delivering responsive, high-quality service in dynamic, high-use environments. As a work lead, the position assists with coordinating daily assignments, monitoring service quality, and supporting staff training. This role requires independent judgment to prioritize work across diverse facility types while adhering to established custodial, safety, and sustainability standards. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Custodial Operations & Facility Maintenance – 75% Perform comprehensive cleaning and sanitation of diverse campus facilities, including classrooms, research laboratories, offices, student centers, dining facilities, recreation areas, and public gathering spaces. Maintain restrooms, instructional spaces, lab environments, food service areas, and high-traffic common spaces with attention to sanitation, safety, and presentation standards. Execute both routine and rapid-response cleaning to address spills, high occupancy impacts, laboratory requirements, and customer service needs in real time. Clean and maintain floors, fixtures, furnishings, windows, and specialized surfaces using established methods and APPA-aligned standards. Remove waste and recycling materials, including high-volume disposal needs in dining, lab, and event environments. Replenish custodial, sanitation, and consumable supplies to ensure uninterrupted service across varied building types. Identify and report maintenance, safety, or environmental concerns, particularly in specialized spaces such as labs and high-use facilities. Utilize CMMS (TMA) and departmental systems to manage assignments, document work, and support operational reporting. Apply sustainable practices and ensure proper chemical handling in alignment with safety standards, including considerations for lab and dining environments. Independently prioritize work based on building schedules, research activity, events, and customer demand across multiple facility types. Event Support, Work Leadership & Team Coordination– 20% Prepare, maintain, and restore spaces for campus events across academic and non-academic facilities, including classrooms, auditoriums, student centers, and dining/event venues. Provide real-time custodial support during events, ensuring spaces remain clean, safe, and responsive to participant needs. Serve as a work lead by coordinating daily custodial assignments across varied environments with competing priorities. Inspect completed work to ensure compliance with custodial, sanitation, and presentation standards across all facility types. Assist with onboarding and training of new employees on procedures, safety protocols, and expectations for both academic and public-facing spaces. Coordinate coverage and communicate staffing or operational gaps due to absences, events, or fluctuating building usage. Provide backup operational leadership in the absence of a Custodian III or supervisor. Equipment Maintenance & Operational Readiness – 2% Inspect, troubleshoot, and perform minor maintenance on custodial equipment to support operations across multiple facility types. Maintain chemical dilution systems and ensure proper functionality, particularly in environments with specialized sanitation needs (labs, dining areas). Identify equipment issues and escalate repair needs to ensure minimal disruption to cleaning operations. Seasonal Support & Emergency Response – 1% Perform snow removal, ice mitigation, and exterior safety support for academic buildings, residence-adjacent areas, and high-traffic public entrances. Respond as essential personnel to emergencies, weather events, and urgent operational needs impacting campus safety and continuity. May be required to work evenings, weekends, and holidays based on operational needs. Professional Development & Additional Duties – 2% Participate in required safety, custodial, and specialized training (including lab safety and sanitation practices where applicable). Apply training to improve efficiency, safety compliance, and service quality across varied campus environments. Contribute to continuous improvement initiatives that enhance customer experience and operational effectiveness within Facilities Services. Perform other duties as assigned to support Facilities Services operations. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: 9/25/2026 Potential interview dates: 10/5/2026 - 10/16/2026 Potential start date: 11/1/2026 - 11/15/2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40981&lang=en": {
      "title": "Materials, Acquisition, and Distribution Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 11, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-FAC-ADMIN OP Schedule: Full-time Materials, Acquisition, and Distribution Manager Facilities Services Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier education al institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Materials, Acquisitions & Distribution Manager to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 64,086.00 - $ 74,767.00 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Materials, Acquisitions & Distribution (MAD) Manager oversees the daily operations of the university's materials management, warehouse, inventory, distribution, procurement support, surplus property, mail services, and logistics functions. This position is responsible for leading a diverse team that supports the acquisition, receiving, storage, tracking, distribution, and disposition of materials, equipment, supplies, and assets necessary to maintain efficient campus operations. The MAD Manager oversees campus-wide warehouse and distribution operations; inventory and asset management programs; surplus property and auction liquidation activities; mailroom services; furniture redistribution; office relocations; e-waste disposal; and event logistics support. Working collaboratively with Facilities Services departments, Business & Finance Solutions, Planning, Design & Construction, campus stakeholders, and external vendors, this position ensures the timely acquisition and availability of materials, equipment, and resources needed to support maintenance, custodial, grounds, utilities, construction projects, and other operational activities. The position works closely with CU System Procurement Services and utilizes established procurement methods to facilitate efficient purchasing and delivery processes, maintain operational continuity, ensure compliance with university policies and procurement requirements, and promote responsible stewardship of university resources. The Materials, Acquisitions & Distribution (MAD) Manager provides leadership and oversight for departmental staff and daily operations, including work planning, process development, inventory management, budget monitoring, warehouse and mailroom services, and customer support functions. The position establishes operational priorities, coordinates service delivery, and identifies opportunities to enhance efficiency, effectiveness, and customer satisfaction in support of university operations. The MAD Manager develops, implements, and maintains operational procedures, service standards, inventory controls, warehouse workflows, and performance metrics that promote accountability, operational excellence, resource stewardship, and continuous improvement across materials management, distribution, logistics, and mail services functions. The position also leads the implementation, administration, and ongoing optimization of inventory and warehouse management functions within the TMA Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS), ensuring accurate inventory records, asset tracking, data integrity, and effective inventory control practices. As a member of the Facilities Services leadership team, the MAD Manager contributes to operational planning, budget oversight, performance reporting, and departmental decision-making, while serving as designated essential personnel during campus emergencies, severe weather events, and operational disruptions to support emergency response, recovery efforts, and continuity of critical campus services. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Supervise and lead the Materials, Acquisitions & Distribution (MAD) team, including work planning, staffing, performance management, training, employee development, and daily operational oversight. Establish departmental priorities, assign and monitor workloads, develop procedures and service standards, ensure compliance with university policies and safety requirements, manage departmental budgets and resources, and foster a culture of customer service, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement in support of campus operations and Facilities Services objectives. Managing campus material procurement, receiving, inventory, storage, and distribution processes working closely with Business & Finance Solutions, Facilities Services operations, Planning, Design, & Construction, CU System Procurement Services, and UCCS stakeholders, and outside vendors. Coordinate and procure parts, tools, equipment, materials, and operational supplies for Facilities Services departments, including Maintenance, Custodial, Grounds, Projects, and Utilities. Research product options, obtain quotes, process purchases, maintain supplier relationships, and ensure timely availability of materials to support daily operations, preventive maintenance, and capital projects. Respond to urgent and emergency purchasing needs by sourcing critical parts and services, expediting deliveries, and coordinating with vendors and department personnel to minimize operational disruptions and maintain continuity of campus services. Manage the end-to-end materials acquisition and distribution function for the university, including procurement coordination, receiving and inspection of goods, inventory control, warehouse operations, storage management, and campus-wide distribution of materials, equipment, and supplies. Maintain accurate inventory records, monitor stock levels, coordinate replenishment activities, ensure proper handling and storage of assets, and support departments with timely delivery of operational and project-related materials. Oversee receiving procedures, surplus inventory utilization, asset tracking, and internal material transfers to maximize efficiency, reduce waste, and support uninterrupted campus operations. Overseeing surplus property, furniture redistribution, office moves, and equipment transfers across campus. Coordinating e-waste collection, asset disposition, and regulatory-compliant disposal of university equipment. Supporting campus events through logistics, furniture delivery, setup, and coordination with Event Services. Developing procedures, service communications, and ensuring efficient customer service to campus departments. Managing budgets, vendor relationships, purchasing activities, and operational reporting. Ensuring compliance with university policies, safety requirements, and asset management standards. Administer surplus asset liquidation program, including identifying surplus property, coordinating asset disposition, ensuring compliance with university policies, maximizing asset recovery value, and maintaining required sales and inventory records. Oversee warehouse operations and inventory management, including storage and tracking of overstock materials, surplus assets pending liquidation, departmental property, and campus inventory; ensure organization, accurate records, asset accountability, and efficient distribution to support university operations. Develop, monitor, and report departmental Key Performance Indicators (KPIs); manage departmental operations and staff performance; attend regular leadership and management meetings; and provide operational updates, metrics, and recommendations to Facilities Services leadership to support informed decision-making. Lead the implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of the inventory and warehouse management modules in the TMA computerized maintenance management system (CMMS). Direct system configuration, process development, testing, deployment, and user adoption; establish and maintain inventory management procedures, asset tracking standards, stock controls, warehouse workflows, and data governance practices to support efficient and accountable Facilities Services operations. Oversee the operation of the university mailroom, including management of incoming and outgoing mail, package receipt and distribution, bulk mail services, postage administration, and delivery logistics. Ensure timely and accurate processing of campus mail and parcels; maintain compliance with USPS and university policies; manage mailroom equipment, vendor relationships, and service contracts; supervise mailroom staff and workflows; and provide responsive customer service to support the communication and operational needs of university departments. Serve as designated essential personnel during weather events and campus emergencies, coordinating snow response operations, supporting disaster recovery activities, procuring emergency supplies and services, and ensuring continuity of critical campus operations. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: 9/25/2026 Potential interview dates: 10/5/2026 - 10/16/2026 Potential start date: 11/1/2026 - 11/15/2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40982&lang=en": {
      "title": "Basic Needs Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 8, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Dean Of Students Schedule: Full-time Basic Needs Coordinator Office of the Dean of Students Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Basic Needs Coordinator to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $44,729 - $57,715 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Office of the Dean of Students cultivates student success through student support and advocacy, educational opportunities, and the promotion of personal accountability and empowerment. The Office of the Dean of Students' addresses issues of students’ safety and wellbeing, and we support all students in times of challenge and crisis. The Basic Needs Coordinator, in collaboration with CARE Team and campus/community partners, will support the basic needs program to meet the needs of under-resourced and high-need students. At the direction of the Assistant Dean of Students/CARE Team and Student Support Director, the Basic Needs Coordinator will oversee programs and provide services, information, and resource referrals related to food, housing, and financial security, as well as other student needs as determined through needs assessments. This position is dependent on the availability of funding. Funding is currently expected to last 3 years. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (35%) Basic Needs Program Coordination & Student Support Coordinate and administer the university's Basic Needs Program to assist students experiencing food insecurity, housing instability, financial hardship, and other basic needs challenges. Meet individually with students to assess needs, provide resource navigation, coordinate referrals, and assist with applications for public benefits and other support programs. Maintain comprehensive knowledge of campus, local, state, and federal resources to ensure timely and appropriate referrals. Coordinate and oversee food security initiatives, including Clyde's Cupboard, Mountain Lion Meals, Fresh Food Friday, the Gift Card Program, and other basic needs initiatives. Monitor student participation and service utilization to identify trends, emerging needs, and opportunities for program enhancement. Maintain confidential student records and documentation in accordance with university policies and applicable regulations. (25%) Program Administration & Operational Support Coordinate daily program operations, including scheduling, inventory oversight, and logistical support for Basic Needs initiatives. Supervise graduate assistants, student employees, and volunteers supporting Clyde's Cupboard and related Basic Needs programs, including training, work assignments, and performance feedback. Compile and maintain information regarding campus emergency funding resources and coordinate with campus partners regarding available assistance programs. Maintain records, prepare reports, and support compliance with university policies, procedures, and reporting requirements. Perform other duties related to the Office of the Dean of Students, CARE Team, and student support operations as assigned. (20%) Partnership Development & Community Collaboration Develop, maintain, and strengthen collaborative relationships with campus departments, community organizations, government agencies, and nonprofit partners to expand student access to basic needs resources. Coordinate with CARE Team members, the Assistant Dean of Students, and campus stakeholders to ensure an integrated approach to student support. Maintain partnerships that promote equitable access to services for historically underserved and under-resourced student populations. Coordinate with community partners to maintain current resource offerings and facilitate collaboration opportunities. Serve as a liaison between students and internal/external resource providers to improve access and reduce barriers to services. (20%) Outreach, Education & Program Assessment Plan, coordinate, and facilitate presentations, workshops, trainings, and outreach activities to increase awareness of Basic Needs services among students, faculty, staff, and community partners. Collaborate with university communications and campus partners to promote available programs and services through multiple communication channels. Maintain and regularly update the Basic Needs website and community resource directory to ensure information remains accurate, accessible, and comprehensive. Participate in ongoing program assessment, student needs assessments, and data collection efforts to evaluate program effectiveness and recommend continuous improvements. Assist with the development and implementation of strategies that strengthen student awareness, utilization, and success outcomes related to Basic Needs services. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: 09/23/2026 Potential interview dates: 10/06/2026 - 10/16/2026 Potential start date: 11/01/2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40301&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Human Physiology and Nutrition",
      "description": "Posted Date: Sep 4, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Beth-El Human Physio/Nutrition Schedule: Full-time The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position Assistant Teaching Professor Department of Human Physiology and Nutrition Helen and Arthur E. Johnson Beth-El College of Nursing and Health Sciences Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an Assistant Teaching Professor to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 50,000 - $55,000 p er academic year. Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt fr om the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Benefits at a Glance Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! CU advantage Summary This is a 9-month, non-tenure track instructional, research, and clinical (IRC) appointment with an anticipated start date of January 2027 . The workload is approximately 80% teaching (24 credit/contact hours) and 20% service. This position has 0% time in research. Teaching responsibilities will be assigned based on departmental needs and include, but are not limited to, Professions in Health Care and Pathophysiology. The ideal candidate will serve as the departmental health professions coordinator/advisor and is expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to collaboration and collegiality across all aspects of faculty engagement. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Collaborate with faculty to design, implement, and deliver an integrated curriculum t hat connects foundational science with clinical applications. Ensure consistency and quality across multiple lecture and laboratory sections each semester. Utilize diverse, evidence-based teaching strategies, including large- and small-group instruction, demonstrations, discussions, simulation, peer instruction, problem-based learning, and team-based learning. Incorporate and effectively use state-of-the-art instructional technologies in both lectures and laboratory settings. Potentially coordinate departmental advising efforts and mentor undergraduate, post-baccalaureate, and graduate students as they prepare for professional schools and careers in healthcare. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will b e given to applications submitted by: October 4, 2026. Potential interview dates: October 12 - November 13, 2026. Potential start date: January 2027. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40574&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Sports Nutrition",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 28, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Beth-El Human Physio/Nutrition Schedule: Part-time The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position Assistant Teaching Professor, Sports Nutrition Department of Human Physiology and Nutrition Helen and Arthur E. Johnson Beth-El College of Nursing and Health Sciences Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an Assistant Teaching Professor (50% time) to joi n our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary R ange : $ 25 ,000 - $27,500 per academic year. Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt fro m the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location : Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer full time employees: Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary This 9-month .5 FTE position is set to begin January 2027. The assistant teaching professor is expected to teach approximately 12 credit hours of undergraduate and/or graduate-level courses in nutrition and sports nutrition each academic year (lectures and labs); mentor undergraduate and graduate students in and outside of the classroom, engage with partner organizations; participate in both internal and external professional service activities; and demonstrate collaborative interests and collegiality in all aspects of university and community engagement. Candidates with expertise in the areas of nutrition, exercise science and other affiliated fields are encouraged to apply. Applicants should possess good interpersonal and communication skills, including proficiency in English. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Teaching & Instruction (80%) Develop and deliver high-quality undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the assigned discipline, using evidence-based teaching practices to promote student learning and engagement. Design course syllabi, assignments, and assessments aligned with program learning outcomes and accreditation standards. Facilitate classroom, laboratory, and/or online instruction using appropriate pedagogical strategies and technology tools. Provide timely and constructive feedback on student work to support academic success. Maintain regular office hours and academic advising for students to guide course selection, career planning, and academic progress. Integrate experiential learning opportunities (e.g., internships, projects, simulations) where appropriate to enhance applied knowledge. Mentor graduate students in capstone projects in nutrition and/or sports nutrition. Continuously update course content to reflect current research, industry trends, and best practices in the field. Examples of courses that may be taught: HPNU 1050: Personal Nutrition; HPNU 2050: Nutrition for Health Professionals; HPNU 3330: Sports Nutrition; HPNU 4060: Advanced Sports Nutrition; HPNU 6900: Nutrition Seminar. Serv ice (20%) Participate in departmental, college, and university committees to support governance, curriculum development, and strategic initiatives. Engage in student recruitment and retention activities, including tours, outreach events and program promotion. Collaborate with colleagues on program assessment and accreditation processes to ensure compliance and continuous improvement. Contribute to community and professional service through partnerships, guest lectures, or involvement in relevant organizations. Mentor adjunct faculty or graduate teaching assistants to maintain instructional quality and consistency. Assist in organizing departmental events, seminars, and workshops that enhance student and faculty engagement. Percentages reflect typical workload but may vary by semester. This role emphasizes instructional excellence and student success, requiring independent judgment in curriculum design and classroom management. Decision-making involves selecting appropriate teaching methods, resolving student concerns, and contributing to departmental policy discussions. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to appl ications submitted by: September 20, 2026. Potential interview dates: October 5-16, 2026. Potential start date: January 2027. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40853&lang=en": {
      "title": "Patron Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Chanc-Ent-Ent Center Admin Schedule: Full-time Patron Services Supervisor Ent Center for the Arts Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement, and is actively seeking a Patron Services Supervisor to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary/Pay Range : $ 41,347 - $ 47,349 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Available twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Patron Services Supervisor supports the Ent Center for the Arts by overseeing daily box office and front-desk operations to ensure exceptional service and efficiency. This position supervises Patron Services Assistants, provides high-visibility customer service, and maintains consistent application of building procedures and ticketing policies. The role serves as a key operational leader during business hours and performances, coordinating closely with the Patron Services Manager, House Management, and Operations leadership. The Supervisor ensures accurate ticketing, reporting, and cash-handling processes while maintaining a welcoming, service-forward environment for all Ent Center programs. This position contributes directly to the Ent Center’s mission by upholding high standards of hospitality, communication, and compliance. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (40%) Patron Services & Operational Leadership Serve as manager on duty for daily front desk and box-office operations, ensuring smooth, service‑oriented patron experiences. Address patron needs, ticketing issues, service escalations, collaborating with the Patron Services Manager, House Manager, and Director of Operations as needed. Maintain comprehensive knowledge of all upcoming Ent Center events and programs; ensure staff are informed through updated Trello boards and shift communications. Oversee cash‑handling procedures, ensuring accurate deposits, proper training, and timely submission of financial materials. Ensure the front desk and shared workspaces meet cleanliness and organizational standards. (35%) Staff Supervision, Training & Scheduling Directly supervise 8–10 hourly Patron Services Assistants, ensuring appropriate staffing for business hours and all performances/events. Manage scheduling and timekeeping using When to Work, On the Clock, and MyLeave, including timesheet approval and shift coverage adjustments. Develop and deliver training on customer service, building policies, front‑desk procedures, and Tessitura ticketing functions. Review and respond to daily shift reports, elevating issues and ensuring follow‑through on operational concerns. (15%) Ticketing, Reporting & System Management Assist with box office setup, event builds, and post‑show revenue settlement in Tessitura. Update online ticketing pages (TNEW) and support voucher creation and complimentary ticket tracking for internal events. Pull basic reports to support internal events, revenue tracking, and operational decision‑making. Process ticket transactions, subscription sales, event registrations, and patron communications as needed. (10%) Patron Communication & Administrative Support Prepare and send performance‑specific patron communications using Prospect 2 automation tools. Support general administrative tasks, including answering phones, responding to emails, and maintaining office supplies. Provide on‑site support during high‑profile or high‑volume event nights to ensure seamless operations. Perform other duties as assigned to support the Patron Services Manager and overall Ent Center operations. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: Friday, September 11th 2026 . Potential interview dates: September 21st 2026 - September 25th 2026 Potential start date: Monday, October 5th 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40851&lang=en": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 26, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCEMSA-Wellness Cent./HS&MHS Schedule: Part-time Front Office Administrative Assistant Wellness Center Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a PART TIME Front Office Administrative Assistant to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $20,446.44 - $26,382.50 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is expected to work 20 hours a week. This position is Non-Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Covering the front desk, which includes: Greeting and checking in and outpatients/clients Answering phone calls Scheduling appointments Answering questions and directing people to the proper resources. Collecting patient/client payments, preparing tickets in Electronic Medical Record and providing walkout receipts to patients/clients. Collecting and entering student immunization records into student information system and assisting with immunization tracking requirements. File maintenance and purging of inactive charts, including scanning into Electronic Medical Record system. Other duties as assigned. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: August 29, 2026 . Potential interview dates: September 8, 2026 - September 18, 2026 . Potential start date: October 1, 2026 . CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40850&lang=en": {
      "title": "Director of Custodial Services",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 25, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-FAC-ADMIN OP Schedule: Full-time Director of Custodial Services Facilities Services Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Director of Custodial Services to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 57,790 - $ 79,710 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Director of Custodial Services provides strategic leadership, administrative oversight, and operational direction for custodial services across the UCCS campus. This position is responsible for developing and implementing custodial service strategies, workforce plans, performance metrics, quality assurance programs, and resource management practices that support the University's mission, customer service objectives, and facility stewardship goals. The Director oversees campus-wide custodial operations through subordinate supervisors and managers, establishes departmental priorities, recommends resource allocation strategies, and serves as a key advisor to Facilities Services leadership regarding service delivery, workforce effectiveness, operational efficiencies, and long-term custodial planning. The position serves as the departmental lead for custodial master planning, campus appearance strategy, sustainability and waste-diversion initiatives, service-level optimization, and performance benchmarking. The position develops long-range operational plans, establishes key performance indicators, and utilizes industry benchmarking through APPA and peer institutions to guide continuous improvement, resource stewardship, and strategic decision-making. The position collaborates extensively with campus leadership, auxiliary units, Housing, Event Services, Public Safety, Environmental Health & Safety, and Facilities partners to ensure safe, effective, and customer-focused custodial programs. The Director may act on behalf of the Executive Director in matters related to custodial operations and service continuity. The Director responds to campus emergencies, supports weather-related operations, and serves as a key technical resource during outages or system failures. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: (30%) Strategic Leadership and Department Administration Develop and implement the long-term strategic vision for custodial services supporting the university's educational mission. Lead the development and maintenance of a comprehensive Custodial Services Master Plan that aligns staffing models, service levels, facility growth, deferred maintenance needs, and institutional priorities. Establish departmental goals, service standards, performance measures, and operational priorities. Develop multi-year operational plans addressing workforce constraints, changing facility utilization, and campus expansion. Recommend policies, procedures, and process improvements that enhance organizational effectiveness and service delivery. Participate in Facilities Services strategic planning and organizational initiatives. Serve as a member of the Facilities Services leadership team. Act on behalf of the Executive Director as delegated. (15%) Workforce and Organizational Leadership Direct and oversee custodial supervisors and operational leadership staff. Develop succession planning, employee engagement, and workforce development programs. Establish and maintain a comprehensive custodial performance management program utilizing key performance indicators (KPIs), operational dashboards, and outcome-based metrics. Benchmark departmental performance against APPA standards and peer higher education institutions to identify opportunities for service enhancement and operational efficiencies. Lead recruitment, retention, organizational development, and workforce planning initiatives. Foster a culture of safety, customer service, continuous improvement, and operational excellence. Lead and oversee custodial staff during weather related and emergency events to include snow/ice mitigation. (15%) Financial Management and Resource Planning Develop, monitor, and manage custodial operating budgets. Lead service-level planning and workforce deployment strategies to maximize service delivery with available staffing resources. Evaluate staffing models and operational efficiencies to ensure sustainable service delivery within budgetary and labor constraints. Develop recommendations for adjusting APPA service levels based on workforce availability, facility priorities, risk assessments, and institutional goals. Oversee equipment replacement planning, custodial capital requests, and long-range resource forecasting. Manage custodial supply needs, service contracts, and vendor performance. Work with the Materials, Acquisition and Distribution Manager and vendors to streamline department ordering and delivery processes. (15%) Campus Partnerships and Stakeholder Engagement Serve as the primary Facilities Services representative for custodial operations. Collaborate with university leadership, academic departments, Housing, Auxiliary Services, and campus partners. Lead planning efforts for support of major campus events and special operational initiatives. Resolve complex service concerns and escalate issues requiring executive attention. Represent Facilities Services on campus committees and working groups. (10%) Operational Performance and Quality Assurance Provide leadership for campus custodial sustainability initiatives in partnership with Facilities Services, Sustainability, and Auxiliary departments. Evaluate performance using APPA levels of cleanliness and key performance indicators. Direct quality assurance programs and operational audits. Lead development of the campus appearance strategy to ensure facilities present a safe, clean, welcoming, and mission-supportive environment. Establish cleanliness, appearance, and facility presentation standards that enhance campus experience for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Evaluate emerging sustainable cleaning technologies, products, and industry best practices for potential implementation. Analyze service data and develop corrective action plans. Lead continuous improvement initiatives focused on service quality, productivity, employee engagement, and customer satisfaction. (10%) Technology and Innovation Provide executive oversight of custodial technology systems and CMMS programs. Leads the development, implementation, and execution of a new CMMS Custodial Module, ensuring effective integration into campus work order and facility management systems. Establish performance reporting and dashboard metrics. Lead implementation of new technologies, automation opportunities, and operational innovations. Direct development of custodial workflows and service delivery optimization initiatives. (5%) Emergency Management and Business Continuity Provide leadership during campus emergencies and severe weather events. Coordinate department response and continuity planning. Serve within Facilities Services incident command structures as assigned. Ensure preparedness plans, training, and resource deployment strategies are maintained. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: 9/9/2026 Potential first round interview dates: 9/17/2026 - 9/25/2026 Potential second round interview dates: 9/28/2026 - 10/6/2026 Potential start date: 11/1/2026 . CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40854&lang=en": {
      "title": "Simulation Senior Professional",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 21, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Beth-El UG Nursing Schedule: Part-time Simulation Senior Professional Department of Nursing Helen and Arthur E. Johnson Beth-El College of Nursing and Health Sciences Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Simulation Senior Professional to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Pay Range : $ 25,086.53 - $32,369 annually at .49 FTE . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications.This position is Non-Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We offer full time employees (1.0 FTE) the following, and some part-time employees a prorated version: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Helen and Arthur E. Johnson Beth-El College of Nursing and Health Sciences at the University of Colorado Colorado Springs is a distinguished and innovative college providing excellence in education, scholarship, and practice in the health professions, offering undergraduate and graduate degrees, and facilitating collaboration for the promotion of a healthy community. The primary responsibilities of this position are to independently prepare, manage, operate and maintain all equipment needed for the delivery of simulation learning in the college Simulation Learning Center (SLC) with a focus on advanced operation of high-fidelity computerized human simulators. This position will serve as an experienced, knowledgeable professional resource as a coequal member of the SLC administrative team. This role is part-time (19 hours per week) and is not eligible for benefits. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Problem Solving Troubleshoots and maintains highly technical computerized simulators and independently assesses the appropriateness of different solutions based on professional knowledge and manufacturer recommendations. Identifies problems/malfunctions with other clinical equipment, examines and repairs or reports as appropriate. Analyze software and hardware applications and peripherals across the domain of high fidelity simulation for conflicts and failrues and provide professional insight into root causes, fixes, and preventative solutions. Simulation Preparation Independently ensures that the Simulation Learning Center is prepared to professionally execute simulation scenarios for learners across the spectrum from undergraduate to doctoral level students. Performs advanced-level programming of high-fidelity simulations to maintain a consistently high level of medical realism. Independently ensure supplies for specific events are staged, including installation of fluids to compartments of simulators and determine the appropriate moulage and props needed to increase realism of the simulator. Equipment & Supplies Independently tracks and schedules periodic maintenance, and repairs of task trainers, simulators, and other simulation equipment, performing such tasks in-house as the position deems appropriate. Maintains cleanliness and order of specialized equipment and supplies. Works as a co-equal member of the SLC administrative team to track supplies and equipment needs and to order supplies in preparation for upcoming simulations. Simulation Daily Operations Independently operate high-fidelity simulators at an advanced level and provide training to others in that professional domain. Identifies issues with the operation of simulation days and provides professional insight and guidance to the rest of the SLC administrative team in how to mitigate those concerns. Provides management, oversight and support for Student Simulation Technicians throughout the simulation day. Participates in orientation of students/faculty to the Simulation Learning Center. Occasionally acts as a patient, family member, or care provider in some scenarios. Independently determines the appropriateness of storage and maintenance options and ensures that supplies and equipment are dismantled and/or stored following events including routine cleaning and maintenance of the medical manikins. Personal Growth Maintains the attitude of a continual learner. Stays current with the developments in the field of Simulation Technology. Participates in conferences and seminars. Attends meetings and contributes to committee work as a professional member of the College. Tentative Search Timeline Priority wi ll be given to applications submitted by : August 26, 2026 Potential interview dates: August 31 - September 11, 2026 Potential start date: October 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40865&lang=en": {
      "title": "COB Academy Facilitator (pool)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 19, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: BUS-Administrative Ops Schedule: Part-time COB Academy Facilitator (pool) College of Business Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! *** This is an evergreen COB Academy Facilitator Pool. This posting is to create a pool of applicants. Please note that we will contact qualified individuals as needed to teach courses.*** Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a COB Academy Facilitator (pool) to join our team! UCCS offers a diverse and inclusive learning environment that fosters innovation, growth, and the holistic development of its students. Compensation: This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Course Facilitation: $62.25 - 199.75 per student completion based on whether the course is a micro-course or an online course. The compensation for in-person courses vary by course length. Course Development: $666.50 - $2,000 for course development based on whether the course is a micro-course or an online course. The compensation for in-person courses will vary based on the contact hours. This position may be eligible for paid sick leave. Information on benefits, including eligibility, is located at: http://www.cu.edu/employee-services . Work Location : Determined by course modality: in-person or online as determined by the course offering. Summary The College of Business at the University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) will establish and maintain a pool of COB Academy Facilitators from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure track positions will be made. Appointments are part-time (less than 50% time) and will be made as courses are offered. This position will teach and/or facilitate non-credit business courses through the COB Academy. COB Academy is a non-traditional, non-credit professional development and lifelong learning program for students, alumni, and community members through a micro-credential and certificate platform. Courses may be in-person or online, depending on the course offering. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position may include, but are not limited to: Develop and design non-credit business courses for COB Academy. Facilitate high-quality content to non-credit learners. Facilitate student learning by providing guidance and timely responses to questions. Create, maintain, and coordinate engaging learning experiences that support the achievement of desired learning outcomes. Design and implement assessment and evaluation tools to measure student progress and achievement of course learning objectives. Utilize learning management systems (e.g., Brightspace) to support course delivery, student engagement, and learning assessment, for online courses. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the College of Business. This is a revolving COB Academy Facilitator Pool for the College of Business. If there is a course opening and your qualifications match a course and the minimum requirements, you may be contacted at that time. The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position. The University of Colorado Colorado Springs is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To assist in achieving this goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history check. Applicants with disabilities: If you have a mental or physical impairment, which limits one of your major life activities (e.g. walking, hearing, seeing, speaking, breathing, or learning) and require special accommodations for testing or interviewing, it is your responsibility to notify the office scheduling the interview or test at least 3 working days before the interview or test date. If you need special accommodations at the work site, you must notify the appointing authority or Human Resources. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40845&lang=en": {
      "title": "Emergency Management Program Director",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 17, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-Police Operations Schedule: Full-time Emergency Management Program Director Department of Public Safety Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier education al institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Emergency Management Program Director to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 67,449 - $ 93,033 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary The Emergency Management Program Director at the University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) plays a pivotal role in ensuring a safe and secure campus environment. This position is responsible for the ongoing leadership and oversight of the university's emergency management program, which includes developing and implementing strategic plans that support UCCS's mission . The Program Director is tasked with collaborating with internal and external stakeholders, providing guidance on emergency preparedness, and ensuring the university is well-equipped to handle a variety of emergencies. The position requires strong leadership skills, strategic planning abilities, and a commitment to fostering a culture of safety and preparedness across the university community . Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Leadership and Program Oversight Lead the Emergency Management Program, aligning its objectives with the university's mission and goals. Develop and manage comprehensive emergency preparedness, response, mitigation, and recovery plans tailored to the needs of the UCCS campus. Ensure the program's strategic direction is responsive to the dynamic needs of the university and its community. Strategic Planning and Coordination: Coordinate strategies to assess and manage the impacts of significant natural or human-caused events, such as mass casualty incidents, hazardous material exposures, and natural disasters. Analyze complex interrelationships between multiple governmental and academic institutions to develop tailored emergency management strategies and processes. Training and Community Engagement: Provide training and education to faculty, staff, and students on emergency response plans, the Incident Command System, and other relevant topics through simulations and exercises. Develop guidelines and programs to assist campus constituencies in emergency preparedness and continuity planning, ensuring all community members are equipped to respond effectively. Collaboration and Partnership Development: Serve as a liaison between UCCS and local, state, and federal emergency management agencies to foster partnerships and enhance collaborative efforts. Actively participate in regional emergency preparedness activities and represent UCCS in professional organizations and committees, promoting best practices and shared learning. Resource Management and External Relations: Seek and manage resources, including grants and funding, to support the university's emergency management initiatives. Oversee and coordinate external communications related to emergency management activities, ensuring transparency and alignment with UCCS's strategic objectives . Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: September 1, 2026 . Potential interview dates: September 15 - 22, 2026 Potential start date: October 1, 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40712&lang=en": {
      "title": "IDEA Data Analyst",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 17, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCAF-Inst Data, Eff &Analytics Schedule: Full-time IDEA Data Analyst Office of Institutional Data, Effectiveness, and Analytics Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier education al institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking a Data Analyst to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $ 56,286- $72,627 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: On-Site/Hybrid (This position will need to be on campus 2 days per week.) Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture ! Summary The IDEA Data Analyst supports the Office of Institutional Data, Effectiveness, and Analytics (IDEA) by providing technical expertise in data collection, validation, analysis, reporting, visualization, and survey research to advance institutional effectiveness and data-informed decision-making. The incumbent collaborates with campus partners to develop meaningful reports, dashboards, surveys, and research that support student success, strategic planning, assessment, accreditation, and institutional accountability. Reporting to the Director of Institutional Data, Effectiveness, and Analytics (IDEA), the Data Analyst contributes to institutional research and survey initiatives, promotes data quality and governance practices, and serves as a trusted resource for campus stakeholders. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Data Validation (10%) – Assesses the quality and accuracy of data used by IDEA and attempts to identify root causes of any inconsistencies. Collaborates with appropriate campus data stewards and custodians to resolve the concerns. Documents data definitions, business rules, and reporting processes in alignment with UCCS data governance practices. Supports efforts to maintain reliable institutional data across reporting platforms and institutional datasets. Query Building (10%) – Creates and refines queries to retrieve accurate and current information from institutional data sources (e.g., PeopleSoft/Campus Solutions, CU Central Information Warehouse, Slate, Qualtrics) for use in reports, visualizations, survey administration, research, and analysis. Report Generation and Data Visualization (20%) – Designs, develops, and maintains interactive Tableau dashboards, reports, and visualizations that communicate institutional performance and support data-informed decision-making. Collaborates with stakeholders across Academic Affairs, Student Success, Administration, and other campus units to develop reports that address planning, assessment, accreditation, and operational needs. Assists in maintaining scalable reporting solutions that provide timely, accurate, and actionable information to internal and external stakeholders. Survey Development, Administration, and Analysis (30%) – Serves as the primary administrator for institutional surveys managed by IDEA and supports the development, administration, analysis, and reporting of institutional surveys including NSSE and custom campus surveys. Uses Qualtrics to design, manage, and deploy surveys. Analyzes quantitative and qualitative results, produces reports, visualizations, summaries, and presentations that clearly communicate survey findings for institutional planning, assessment, accreditation, and student success initiatives. Faculty Course Questionnaire (FCQ) Administration (30%) – Serves as the primary administrator for the Watermark Faculty Course Questionnaire (FCQ) system, managing term setup, course, instructor, and student data imports, survey scheduling, communications, and troubleshooting. Collaborates with the Faculty Resource Center on LMS/Canvas integration, the Office of Information Technology, the Office of Faculty Affairs, and other campus stakeholders to maintain and improve FCQ processes, documentation, and recommend workflow enhancements that improve efficiency, data quality, student experience and response rates. The job duties and percentages listed are typical examples of work performed by positions in this job classification and are not intended to represent a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, or tasks. Specific assignments may vary depending on departmental priorities and institutional needs. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: September 1, 2026 . Potential interview dates: September 7, 2026- September 11, 2026 Potential start date: October 1, 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=40721&lang=en": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Development",
      "description": "Posted Date: Aug 6, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCUA-University Development Schedule: Full-time Associate Director of Development University Development Elevate Your Career at UCCS: Innovate, Inspire, and Impact in the Rockies! Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking an Associate Director of Development to join our team! UCCS is committed to academic excellence, professional development, and fostering an environment that supports innovation and student success. At the base of the Rocky Mountains, Colorado Springs is captivated by its stunning landscapes, making it a paradise for nature lovers. This city is more than its scenery—a mosaic of history, arts, and a vibrant tech scene. We invite you to join a community that cherishes outdoor adventure as much as forward-thinking growth, an exceptional setting for both career and lifestyle. Salary Range : $65,734 - $76,689 annually . Compensation will be commensurate upon experience and qualifications. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Work Location: Hybrid Benefits at a Glance At UCCS, our employees are our most valued asset. We're proud to offer: Generous Time Off : Enjoy 22 vacation days, 10 sick days, paid parental leave, 13 recognized holidays, and provisions for bereavement, jury duty, and FAMLI Leave. Robust Health Coverage : Our comprehensive medical plans cover preventative care at no cost, including a yearly mental health visit. Plus, benefit from affordable dental, vision plans, and competitive prescription drug prices. Financial & Retirement Benefits : Take advantage of our health savings, flexible spending accounts, and life and disability insurance. Plan for your future with our retirement options. Further Your Education : Avail twelve (12) waived credits per academic year for courses at any CU campus. We invest in your educational and professional growth. Wellness & More : From wellness programs aimed at achieving your best self to various additional benefits through CU Advantage, we prioritize well-being and holistic development. Want to know your total compensation? Use our calculator to get the complete picture! Summary University Advancement professionals build various levels of support and affinity for the institution through a coordinated effort as part of the university's primary outreach to the community and region. This includes building support and funding through community engagement and alumni outreach efforts, attendance at key events, representation on important initiatives and the creation of partnerships supporting the university's mission. The Associate Director of Development coordinates, directs, and implements philanthropic fundraising activities for the broad campus, scholarships and a select number of assigned campus units. Strong collaborative skills and a team-focused approach is crucial in this role. The Associate Director of Development is responsible for planning, implementing, and coordinating fundraising activities for designated programs and areas. Plans and carries out the institution's program of soliciting major gifts typically between $15K-$25K and higher. This position typically handles mid-level, moderately complex gift prospects, with the intent of cultivating, sustaining, and increasing donor relationships. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Fundraising (75%) Raise philanthropic support for the institution while following the Donor Bill of Rights to achieve established goals. Identify, attract and manage prospective donors, and manage/retain assigned existing donors, leading to additional investments for the benefit of the institution: Solid ability to cultivate and solicit donations at major gift level with strong focus on identifying and cultivating new donors to the institution. Demonstrated experience in successfully managing a donor/client portfolio, preferably in a university setting. Manages portfolio consisting of a minimum of 90-120 prospects. Goals relating to personal contacts, number of proposed gifts, planned gifts, grants, and prospect identification to be set with and approved by management. Works to cultivate existing and new donor relationships (individual, corporate, and foundation) with the intent of sustaining and increasing the relationship with the donor. Collaborate and partner on major giving prospects for complex giving opportunities as appropriate. Works closely with University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) faculty, staff and volunteers daily to develop and implement fundraising strategies and appeals in order to meet established goals and objectives through productive relationships. Able to demonstrate a solid knowledge of fundraising techniques. Proven ability to conduct cold-calls resulting in future support for the institution. Work in concert with fellow Advancement and Engagement Division personnel, and through individual contributions, to effectively execute stewardship activities designed to enhance the relationship between donors and the University. Ability to travel both in and out-of-state (15% out of state, 60% in state). Reporting and Data (15%) Ensure integrity of donor data. Report on annual gift activities and ensure gift programs are in line with CU strategies. Expertly utilize donor database Advance/CU Ascend and similar systems for accurate record maintenance, proposal management, and development of reports to assess/develop donor and other fundraising strategies. Provide necessary documentation and follow-up for donors and internal campus partners as needed. Organizing and coordinating projects and events (10%) Represents the University at events and community functions in order to support the University to cultivate and steward donors. Supports, coordinates and selective implementation of engagement initiatives tied to strategic priorities. Solid ability to contribute to a team-focused advancement and engagement division. Tentative Search Timeline Priority will be given to applications submitted by: August 23, 2026 Potential interview dates: Starting August 25 - September 8, 2026 Potential start date: October 1, 2026 CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=36312&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Space Cyber Enterprise Management (pool)",
      "description": "Posted Date: Jul 24, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: BUS-Administrative Ops Schedule: Part-time Lecturer - Space Cyber Enterprise Management (pool) College of Business Engage. Educate. Empower. Join UCCS as a Lecturer! This is an evergreen Lecturer Pool for the College of Business at UCCS. Applications will be reviewed on a semester-by-semester basis as business needs arise. Who We Are The University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) is a premier educational institution that prides itself on academic excellence, research, and community engagement and is actively seeking Lecturer - Space Cyber Enterprise Management (pool) to join our team! UCCS offers a diverse and inclusive learning environment that fosters innovation, growth, and the holistic development of its students. Pay Range : $4,000 for a 3-credit hour undergraduate course. $4,500 for a 3-credit hour graduate course. This position is Exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) overtime provisions. Because this appointment is temporary in nature, you will not be eligible to receive all of the benefits normally provided to faculty under the standard University of Colorado benefits programs . You are not eligible to receive paid vacation leave, medical, or retirement benefits. However, you are eligible to accrue sick leave at 0.034 hours of sick leave per hour worked. Work Location : Determined by course modality: On-campus, online, or hybrid. Remote teaching opportunities may be available under certain conditions. Summary The College of Business and Administration at the University of Colorado Colorado Springs (UCCS) will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Space Cyber Enterprise Management from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure track positions will be made. Appointments are part-time (less than 50% time) and will be made semester-by-semester. This position will teach classes in the areas of space cyber enterprise management. Classes may be on-campus, online, or hybrid. This is a revolving Lecturer Pool for the College of Business. If there is a course opening and your qualifications match a course and the minimum requirements, you may be contacted at that time. The University of Colorado Colorado Springs will not sponsor work visas or permanent resident applications for this position. Essential Functions The duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Provides instruction to undergraduate/graduate students both in-person and online courses. Maintains, develop and schedules student learning experiences to achieve desired learning outcomes. Plans, develops, and implements evaluation tools to assess student process towards course learning objectives. Be familiar with learning management systems, such as Canvas. Other duties as determined by the College of Business. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. This position does not include new visa sponsorship for individuals outside the U.S. Candidates must already be in the United States with valid work authorization or an employment-based visa. The university will not initiate sponsorship for those who do not currently hold a U.S. work visa or authorization. If you already have valid U.S. work authorization or are on a visa that permits employment, we welcome your application. Applicants should either reside in Colorado or be prepared to relocate within two months of starting employment. We’re excited to welcome new team members and will provide support and resources to help make your transition to Colorado as smooth as possible. The University of Colorado Colorado Springs has implemented a misconduct history check program with respect to final candidates for specific appointments. The misconduct history check program is intended to allow UCCS to collect and review information about a candidate's conduct at their previous institutions, specifically conduct related to sexual misconduct, harassment, and/or discrimination – before making hiring decisions. All final candidates to these appointments are required to complete an Authorization to Release Information and provide contact information for their previous institutions. In accordance with the Equal Pay for Equal Work Act, UCCS does not discriminate based on sex in our employment or compensation practices."
    },
